  "query_preview": "(Saturday through Tuesday)...\nSubstantial drying aloft is expected for Saturday and Sunday.\nPrecipitable water values exceeding 1.5 inch into Friday will\ndecrease to around 1.25 inch on Saturday and 0.75 inch for Sunday\nthrough Tuesday. \n\nIn addition to the drying aloft, high temperatures on Saturday \nwill cool a few to around 5 degrees with another few degrees of\ncooling on Sunday with slight day to day differences for Sunday \nthrough Tuesday. High temperatures for Sunday through Tuesday will\nbe a few degrees below average at lower elevations to around 4 to\n8 degrees below average for the inland valleys. High temperatures\nfor Sunday through Tuesday will range from the 70s near the coast\nto the mid 80s to lower 90s for the Inland Empire with 100 to 104\nfor the lower deserts.\n\nNights will be cooler by Sunday and Monday with low pressure on\nSunday and Monday mostly in the 50s for the inland valleys and in\nthe 60s for coastal areas into the western valleys.",
